      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\nRead it **top to bottom**, the way Google SREs triage a page.\n\n1. **SLOs (top row):** *are players OK?* An SLO (Service Level Objective) is the reliability target we promise, e.g. \"up 99.5% of the time\". The **error budget** is the 0.5% we're *allowed* to fail. Budget left \u2192 ship features. Budget gone \u2192 fix reliability first.\n2. **The four golden signals** (Google SRE book, ch. 6): **Latency** (how slow), **Traffic** (how much), **Errors** (how often it fails), **Saturation** (how full). If you can only watch four things, watch these.\n3. Rule of thumb: **alert on symptoms players feel** (top rows), **debug with causes** (bottom rows). A full CPU nobody notices is not an emergency; a failed join is.\n\n**Low-traffic caveat:** SaucerJam has only a handful of players, so request-based numbers are noisy or empty (\"no players in window\" is normal). That's why the headline availability uses a **synthetic probe**: Prometheus fetches `qd.menezmethod.com/metrics` through Cloudflare every 15s, like a robot player. The SRE workbook recommends this for low-traffic services.\nSources: [SRE book: Monitoring Distributed Systems](https://sre.google/sre-book/monitoring-distributed-systems/) \u00b7 [Workbook: Implementing SLOs](https://sre.google/workbook/implementing-slos/) \u00b7 [Workbook: Alerting on SLOs](https://sre.google/workbook/alerting-on-slos/) \u00b7 [Google Cloud SRE blog](https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/devops-sre) \u00b7 [SRE Weekly](https://sreweekly.com/)"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "SLOs: are players OK? (30-day window)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Availability (probe), 30d",
      "description": "**SLI:** share of 15s probes (Prometheus scraping the public URL through Cloudflare) that succeeded.\n**SLO: 99.5%**, about 3.6 hours of allowed downtime per month.\n**Why 99.5% and not 99.99%?** One free VM, no redundancy, one developer. Google's advice: set the target to what users need and what you can afford, not \"as high as possible\". Each extra nine costs about 10x more work.\n**Why a probe?** Too few players for request-based numbers to mean anything (see the workbook's advice for low-traffic services).\nNote: this job was added to Oracle Prometheus on 2026-09-25, so \"30d\" covers less history until late October.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.995
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "avg_over_time(up{job=\"saucerjam\"}[30d])",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "decimals": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Error budget left, 30d",
      "description": "**Error budget** = 100% minus SLO = 0.5% of the month we're allowed to be down.\nThis panel shows how much of that allowance is left. 100% = untouched, 0% = spent.\n**How to use it (Google's error-budget policy):** budget left \u2192 take risks, ship features, deploy on Fridays. Budget spent \u2192 freeze risky changes and fix reliability. It turns \"is it reliable enough?\" from an argument into a number.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.25
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.5
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "1 - (1 - avg_over_time(up{job=\"saucerjam\"}[30d])) / 0.0050000000000000044",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Burn rate, 1h",
      "description": "**Burn rate** = how fast we're spending the error budget. 1 = exactly on pace to use it all in 30 days. 14.4 = the whole month's budget gone in about 2 days.\nGoogle's **multi-window, multi-burn-rate** alerting pages a human when the 1h burn rate is above **14.4** (2% of the monthly budget in one hour) *and* the 5m burn rate confirms it's still happening.\nWe don't page on this yet (too little traffic, see docs/SRE.md), but this is the number a mature setup would page on.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "x",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 6
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 14.4
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "(1 - avg_over_time(up{job=\"saucerjam\"}[1h])) / 0.0050000000000000044",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Burn rate, 6h",
      "description": "Same idea over 6 hours. The workbook's second paging tier: burn rate above **6** over 6h (5% of the monthly budget) means a slower but real problem.\nTwo windows catch both kinds of failure: sudden outages (1h) and slow leaks (6h).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "x",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 6
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "(1 - avg_over_time(up{job=\"saucerjam\"}[6h])) / 0.0050000000000000044",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Join success, 30d (SLO 99%)",
      "description": "**SLI for the most important player journey: pressing \"Play online\" and getting into a match.**\n= successful joins / (successful joins + joins rejected by the server).\nRejections by `rate_limited` or `debounced` are excluded: those are the server protecting itself from spam clicks, not failures a real player feels.\nMeasure **user journeys**, not servers (Google: \"SLIs should be as close to the user as possible\").\nEmpty = nobody tried to join in the window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "noValue": "no joins in window",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.99
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(saucerjam_joins_total[30d])) / (sum(increase(saucerjam_joins_total[30d])) + (sum(increase(saucerjam_join_failures_total{reason!~\"rate_limited|debounced\"}[30d])) or vector(0)) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Request success, 30d (SLO 99.5%)",
      "description": "**SLI:** share of real HTTP requests (health checks and /metrics excluded) that did *not* return a 5xx.\n**Only 5xx counts as bad.** A 404 from a scanner guessing URLs is the client's fault, not ours. Google counts errors the *service* causes.\nHealth checks are excluded because they're about 99% of all requests and would keep this number at 100% forever.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "noValue": "no requests in window",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.995
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "1 - ((sum(increase(saucerjam_http_requests_total{status=~\"5..\",route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[30d])) or vector(0)) / (sum(increase(saucerjam_http_requests_total{route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[30d])) > 0))",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Fast requests, 30d (SLO 95% < 250ms)",
      "description": "**Latency SLI:** share of real HTTP requests answered in under **250ms**.\n**Why a threshold ratio and not \"average latency\"?** Averages hide pain: 99 fast requests and 1 ten-second one average out to \"fine\". Google recommends \"X% of requests faster than Y\", which also plugs straight into an error budget.\n250ms is one of the histogram's bucket edges, so this is exact, not interpolated.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "noValue": "no requests in window",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.95
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(saucerjam_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{le=\"0.25\",route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[30d])) / (sum(increase(saucerjam_http_request_duration_seconds_count{route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[30d])) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Smooth pings, 30d (SLO 90% < 150ms)",
      "description": "**Game-feel SLI:** share of in-game pings (reported by players' browsers) that round-tripped in under **150ms**.\nFor a real-time shooter, this *is* the latency players feel. Above about 150ms, hits start to feel wrong.\nIt measures the player's network + Cloudflare + our server, so a bad number can be the player's Wi-Fi. That's fine: an SLI measures what the user experiences, whoever is at fault.\nEmpty = nobody played online in the window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 16,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "noValue": "no online play in window",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(saucerjam_ws_round_trip_seconds_bucket{le=\"0.15\"}[30d])) / (sum(increase(saucerjam_ws_round_trip_seconds_count[30d])) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Availability (probe), hourly vs SLO",
      "description": "Hourly probe success rate. Any dip below the dashed line is budget being spent.\nLook for **patterns**: dips at the same time every day usually mean a cron job, backup or deploy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "SLO target"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "avg_over_time(up{job=\"saucerjam\"}[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "availability"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "0.995",
          "legendFormat": "SLO target"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Golden signal 1: Latency (how slow?)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "HTTP latency p50 / p95 / p99 (real requests)",
      "description": "**Percentiles, not averages.** p95 = 95% of requests were faster than this line. p99 = the unlucky 1%.\nTail latency (p99) is what your worst-off players feel, and with many requests per session, most players hit the tail eventually.\nHealth checks excluded. Gaps = no requests.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(saucerjam_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(saucerjam_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(saucerjam_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{route!~\"/health|/metrics\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
